  "tiles": [
    {
      "tile_id": "tile_stats_center_spread",
      "title": "Measures of Center and Spread",
      "summary": "Introduces the three measures of central tendency (mean, median, mode) and three measures of spread (range, variance, standard deviation) using a seven-order QuickRide delivery dataset. Emphasises when the median is more representative than the mean, and why standard deviation is more interpretable than variance.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s01",
          "type": "explainer",
          "concept_ids": [
            "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Measures of Center",
          "title": "What's a typical delivery time?",
          "lede": "Seven QuickRide orders came in at 18, 20, 22, 22, 26, 28, and 80 minutes. Before you can say anything useful, you need one number that answers \"what's typical here?\" — and there are three ways to find it.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "data_table",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s01.b1",
              "asset_ref": {
                "asset_id": "ds_seven_delivery_times",
                "columns": [
                  "order_id",
                  "delivery_time"
                ]
              },
              "caption": "Seven delivery times sorted smallest to largest. Mean ≈ 30.9 min (pulled up by ORD-007), median = 22 min (middle value), mode = 22 min (appears twice).",
              "highlight": [
                {
                  "target": {
                    "kind": "row",
                    "row": {
                      "where": {
                        "order_id": "ORD-007"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "label": "outlier pulls mean up",
                  "tone": "bad"
                },
                {
                  "target": {
                    "kind": "row",
                    "row": {
                      "where": {
                        "order_id": "ORD-003"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "label": "median (4th of 7)",
                  "tone": "focus"
                },
                {
                  "target": {
                    "kind": "row",
                    "row": {
                      "where": {
                        "order_id": "ORD-004"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "label": "mode (22 appears twice)",
                  "tone": "focus"
                }
              ],
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#f1",
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#f2"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb1",
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb2",
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb3"
                ],
                "anchors": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#visual"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s01.b2",
              "role": "definition",
              "text": "The **sample mean** is the sum of all values divided by the count. For these seven orders: 18 + 20 + 22 + 22 + 26 + 28 + 80 = 216, and 216 ÷ 7 ≈ **30.9 minutes**.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#f1"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb2"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s01.b3",
              "role": "definition",
              "text": "The **median** is the middle value of the sorted list. With seven orders, the fourth value is the middle one — that's **22 minutes**. If there were an even number of orders, you'd average the two middle values.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#f2"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb3"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "reward": {
            "gems": 2
          },
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#f1",
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#f2"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb1",
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb2",
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb3"
            ],
            "anchors": [
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#visual"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "step_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s02",
          "type": "explainer",
          "concept_ids": [
            "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Measures of Center",
          "title": "Mode and when the mean misleads",
          "lede": "The mean and median both describe center, but they react very differently when one value is far from the rest.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s02.b1",
              "role": "definition",
              "text": "The **mode** is the value that appears most often. In this batch, 22 minutes appears twice while every other time appears once — so **22 minutes** is the mode. A dataset can have more than one mode.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#f3"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb4"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s02.b2",
              "role": "misconception",
              "text": "Notice the gap: mean ≈ 30.9 min, but median = mode = 22 min. The mean is more strongly affected by extreme observations than the median, which is more robust to them. That single 80-minute delivery pulls the mean almost 9 minutes above where six of the seven orders actually sit. When a dataset has one unusually large value, the median is usually the better \"typical\" number to report.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#f4"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb5"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "reward": {
            "gems": 2
          },
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#f3",
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#f4"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb4",
              "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center#tb5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "step_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s03",
          "type": "check",
          "concept_ids": [
            "stats.descriptive_measures_of_center"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Quick Check",
