        },
        {
          "step_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s05",
          "type": "explainer",
          "concept_ids": [
            "stats.measures_of_spread"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Measures of Spread",
          "title": "How spread out are the delivery times?",
          "lede": "Knowing the median is 22 minutes doesn't say whether all orders are close to that or wildly scattered. Spread measures fill that gap.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s05.b1",
              "role": "intro",
              "text": "Most of the seven delivery times (18, 20, 22, 22, 26, 28, 80 minutes) cluster fairly close together — but one sits far away. The **range** is the simplest spread measure: largest minus smallest. Here that's 80 − 18 = **62 minutes**.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#f1"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#tb1",
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#tb2"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s05.b2",
              "role": "mechanism",
              "text": "The **variance** measures the average squared distance from the mean. With a mean of about 30.9 minutes, the seven squared deviations sum to about 2 886.9. Dividing by n − 1 = 6 gives a variance of about **481.1 minutes²**.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#f2"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#tb3"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "process_flow",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s05.b3",
              "title": "From raw values to standard deviation",
              "direction": "TB",
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "id": "n1",
                  "label": "Each value − mean",
                  "kind": "step",
                  "detail": "deviation (minutes)"
                },
                {
                  "id": "n2",
                  "label": "Square each deviation",
                  "kind": "step",
                  "detail": "squared deviation (minutes²)"
                },
                {
                  "id": "n3",
                  "label": "Sum the squared deviations",
                  "kind": "step",
                  "detail": "≈ 2 886.9 minutes²"
                },
                {
                  "id": "n4",
                  "label": "Divide by n − 1",
                  "kind": "step",
                  "detail": "variance ≈ 481.1 minutes²"
                },
                {
                  "id": "n5",
                  "label": "Take the square root",
                  "kind": "step",
                  "detail": "standard deviation ≈ 21.9 minutes"
                }
              ],
              "edges": [
                {
                  "from": "n1",
                  "to": "n2",
                  "kind": "next"
                },
                {
                  "from": "n2",
                  "to": "n3",
                  "kind": "next"
                },
                {
                  "from": "n3",
                  "to": "n4",
                  "kind": "next"
                },
                {
                  "from": "n4",
                  "to": "n5",
                  "kind": "next"
                }
              ],
              "alt_text": "Five-step flowchart: subtract mean → square → sum → divide by n-1 (variance, minutes²) → square root (standard deviation, minutes).",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#f2"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#tb3"
                ],
                "anchors": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#visual"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "reward": {
            "gems": 2
          },
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "stats.measures_of_spread"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "stats.measures_of_spread#f1",
              "stats.measures_of_spread#f2"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "stats.measures_of_spread#tb1",
              "stats.measures_of_spread#tb2",
              "stats.measures_of_spread#tb3"
            ],
            "anchors": [
              "stats.measures_of_spread#visual"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "step_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s06",
          "type": "explainer",
          "concept_ids": [
            "stats.measures_of_spread"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Measures of Spread",
          "title": "Standard deviation and the range's blind spot",
          "lede": "The variance is useful for calculation, but its units are squared. The standard deviation brings the number back to the original units — and the range has a hidden weakness.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s06.b1",
              "role": "mechanism",
              "text": "The **standard deviation** is the square root of the variance: √481.1 ≈ **21.9 minutes** — roughly how far a typical delivery time sits from the 30.9-minute mean. It's in the same units as the data, making it easier to interpret than the variance (minutes²).",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#f3"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#tb4"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s06.b2",
              "role": "misconception",
              "text": "The **range** (62 minutes) uses only the two most extreme values and ignores how the rest of the data are spread. Variance and standard deviation use every observation's distance from the mean, so they capture whether the middle values are bunched or scattered.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#f4"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stats.measures_of_spread#tb5"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "reward": {
            "gems": 2
          },
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "stats.measures_of_spread"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "stats.measures_of_spread#f3",
              "stats.measures_of_spread#f4"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "stats.measures_of_spread#tb4",
              "stats.measures_of_spread#tb5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "step_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s07",
          "type": "video",
          "concept_ids": [
            "stats.measures_of_spread"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Watch",
          "title": "Variance and standard deviation, worked by hand",
          "lede": "Watch the squared-deviation method in action, then see why dividing by n − 1 gives a better estimate for a sample.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "media_group",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_center_spread.s07.b1",
              "segment_ids": [
                "seg_stats.measures_of_spread_SzZ6GpcfoQY_236_612"
              ],
              "bridge": {
                "before": "Watch squaring make the units squared and the square root bring them back. The clip first divides by n for a full population, then by n - 1 for a sample; Devspace's variance is the n - 1 version.",
                "after": "The clip never covers the range. Devspace adds it: the range uses only the two extreme values, so it can't say whether the rest of the data is bunched or scattered."
              }
            }
          ],
